    "interpretation": "The pinned R580 PMM path gathers each allocated root chunk tracker, then waits on entries owned by GPUs other than the PMM GPU. The ordinary no-eviction allocation is reached from block population after its VA-block lock assertion; the eviction retry explicitly unlocks that lock before calling the PMM allocator. This proves a conditional lock-held CPU-wait path in source, but does not prove a deadlock. Reachability remains unresolved for the isolated mixed-provider design: no runtime trace establishes that a pending foreign-GPU tracker can reach this PMM path. A simple early error is not justified because the allocator's error path deinitializes the collected tracker and frees chunks; safety with pending GPU work has not been proved.",
